// From the resolution: tricolor of equal bands, 2:3, a navy wheel at the center, of about
// the white band's width, in the design of the wheel on the Sarnath capital.
// From IS 1:1968, Table 6 and Fig. 4, flag size 1, 6300 by 4200 mm:
//   J 1295 outer diameter, K 1120 inside the rim, L 112, N 14
//   24 spokes at 15 degrees, hub diameter 2L, each spoke 3N wide on a circle of 4L,
//     and N wide where it meets the hub
// Derived here from the figure:
//   a spoke tapers 3N to N over L, so it comes to a point at L/2 = 56 from the center,
//     and its outer point is on the K circle, 560. The midpoint of 56 and 560 is 308.
//   L runs from the bottom of a scallop to the wheel's edge, so a scallop's radius is
//     L - (J - K) / 2 = 24.5, centered on the K circle, between the spokes.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "India"
  date "1947-07-22"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://www.constitutionofindia.net/debates/22-jul-1947/"
  source "https://law.resource.org/pub/in/bis/S12/is.1.1968.pdf"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/in.html"
  note "The resolution sets the design. The wheel's construction and the exact 3:2 are IS 1:1968, a Bureau of Indian Standards specification for cotton khadi flags (reaffirmed 2003, read with amendments to No. 4), not a law. The Flag Code of India wasn't read, because the Home Ministry's links failed."
  note "The resolution says 'ordinarily' 2:3, and IS 1 allows other ratios for special purposes, without a rule for them, so none is written here."
  note "IS 1's sleeve, hem and reinforcements are omitted. Its colors are set by a sealed sample at Kanpur, and the CIE values recorded here are its note on the flag of 1947, with brightness as Y."
  note "The hex, Pantone and CMYK values are the Album des Pavillons 2023 as FOTW reports it. White is plain white."
  law "Resolution of the Constituent Assembly of India on the National Flag, 22 July 1947" {
    source "https://www.constitutionofindia.net/debates/22-jul-1947/"
  }
}
palette {
  saffron "#ff671f" {
    pantone "165 C"
    cmyk 0 60 88 0
    reference "IS 1:1968, CIE 1931 xyY, illuminant C" "0.538 0.360 21.5"
  }
  white "#ffffff" {
    reference "IS 1:1968, CIE 1931 xyY, illuminant C" "0.313 0.319 72.6"
  }
  green "#046a38" {
    pantone "349 C"
    cmyk 89 32 92 24
    reference "IS 1:1968, CIE 1931 xyY, illuminant C" "0.288 0.395 8.9"
  }
  navy "#000091" {
    pantone "2738 C"
    cmyk 100 92 21 6
  }
}
proportion hoist=4200 fly=6300

bars saffron white green
charge ring navy {
  radius 647.5
  inner 560
}
charge disc navy {
  radius 112
}
charge path navy {
  d "M21 0L42 336L21 504L0 336Z"
  box "0 0 42 504"
  fly 42
  hoist 504
  at center
  repeat ring count=24 radius=308 turn=#true
}
charge disc navy {
  radius 24.5
  at center
  repeat arc count=24 radius=560 from=7.5 to=352.5
}
